  "lead_raw_text": " The structure of Ce2Zn24Au2 (CeZn12Au) crystallizes in the orthorhombic space group Amm2 (No. 38), with 28 atoms in the unit cell distributed over eight independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis shows Au centers coordinated by six Zn neighbors, while Ce centers have 20 geometric neighbors (12 Zn and 8 Zn/1 Ce). The Zn environments are more varied, including 12-neighbor close-packed-like arrangements and 11- or 12-neighbor coordination, and the periodic neighbor graph forms a single three-dimensional component spanning all 28 sites. Validated polyhedron-sharing analysis reveals corner- and edge-sharing between Au- and Zn-centered polyhedra, as well as corner-, edge-, and face-sharing among Zn-centered polyhedra.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
